            <ArticleTitle>Unusual presentation of ruptured descending thoracic aortic aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>291-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We here report a very unusual presentation of ruptured thoracic aortic aneurysm. In a 50-year-old patient, almost asymptomatic and in stable clinical conditions, the chest radiograph and computed tomography scan revealed a right-sided rupture of a previously undiagnosed thoracic aortic aneurysm. The patient was treated successfully with an emergency surgical procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
